content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-108 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-23110, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage is approximately one drop every two seconds. This matches the manual symptom 'leakage at shaft seal', for which the corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No allowable drip-rate limit is documented, so a numerical pass/fail comparison cannot be made.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is reported as 3.2 mm/s. Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. If the report was measured on that basis, 3.2 mm/s is in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), 'Long-term operation': it is above the Zone A boundary of 2.8, below the Zone C threshold of 4.5, and below Zone D, which begins at 7.1 and is marked 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. It therefore does not meet the highest-severity-zone immediate-stop trigger.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature is 68 °C. The manual specifies housing-surface measurement for bearing temperature, but the evidence supplies no numerical operating or alarm limit. It is therefore not possible to classify 68 °C as high or to decide whether it exceeds the manufacturer's alarm limit. If it is above that alarm limit, SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P2 is assigned for planned repair of the active seal leak; the reported vibration does not require an immediate stop. This priority is provisional until the missing bearing-temperature alarm limit is checked, because an above-alarm temperature would instead trigger P1 within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: early failure of the original HF3-450 component mechanical seal. This asset's serial HF3-23110 is within the SB-2026-014 population (HF3-22000 and above), where field returns identify early HF3-450 failure caused by a revised sleeve tolerance. The manual also identifies worn or cracked seal faces as a probable cause of shaft-seal leakage. Confirm the installed seal and failure mode during strip-down.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other documented seal-leakage causes are the seal having run dry and shaft misalignment. The evidence does not distinguish between them; check alignment as part of the corrective work. A Zone B vibration reading alone does not diagnose misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before starting, obtain the manufacturer's bearing-housing temperature alarm limit and compare it with a housing-surface temperature reading. Escalate to P1 within the shift if the reading is above the alarm limit. Also confirm chemical-dosing status and lifting weights so the conditional safety controls can be applied.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting and before breaking into the pump or seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly; its design allows removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve. Identify the installed seal and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; do not fit a replacement HF3-450 seal on this serial-numbered pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge mechanical seal and one new HF3-120 casing gasket. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting; this does not eliminate the separate sleeve-scoring inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the fasteners. For this asset, tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, not the superseded 25 Nm value. Other applicable Table 5 torques, for lightly oiled threads, are: M24 impeller nut 160 Nm, M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm if disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool as part of the seal-leak corrective action and after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At any subsequent running check, assess vibration as mm/s RMS on the bearing housings. If it enters the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set; required replacement for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22000 and above, including HF3-23110.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit a new gasket during mechanical-seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve — conditional allowance of one: replace only if inspection shows scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For this seal/internal pump work, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate both the suction and discharge valves before starting the work.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain a line-break permit; drain and vent before breaking into the pump or seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any component to be lifted weighs more than 25 kg, use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment. Component weights are not supplied, so this control is conditional pending confirmation.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the raw-water line is chemically dosed, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The evidence identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line as chemically dosed but does not establish the dosing status of P-108.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration enters the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The reported 3.2 mm/s, if measured as bearing-housing RMS velocity, is instead in Zone B.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift; whether 68 °C exceeds that limit is currently unknown.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours, for the documented alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Total planned standard labour for seal replacement plus laser alignment is 9.5 technician-hours. Bearing-replacement labour is not included because bearing wear, noise or high temperature has not been established.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-part conflict: the manual parts list identifies HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 prohibits fitting HF3-450 and requires HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward. The bulletin was issued 14 March 2026 and explicitly covers serial HF3-23110, so HF3-450B applies to this asset; pumps below HF3-22000 remain on HF3-450 and the manual instructions.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts and procedure 5.2 refers to Table 5, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Use 30 Nm on this serial-numbered pump with its HF3-450B cartridge seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the manufacturer's applicable HF-300 bearing-housing operating/alarm temperature limit, and does 68 °C exceed it? No numerical temperature limit is included; an above-alarm reading requires P1 within the shift. [C01, C15]",
    "Was the 3.2 mm/s vibration reading recorded as RMS velocity on a bearing housing? The Zone B classification is conditional on those Figure 3 measurement conditions. [C07]",
    "Is there an allowable shaft-seal leakage rate for pre-repair disposition or post-repair acceptance? The evidence supplies only the leakage symptom and corrective action, not a numerical leakage limit. [C09]",
    "Which seal is currently installed, and what scoring depth is found on shaft sleeve HF3-455? Sleeve replacement is required only when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. [C10, C13]",
    "Is the P-108 raw-water line chemically dosed or otherwise subject to the chemical-PPE control? The dosing statement covers P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, not P-108. [C15, C16]",
    "Will any component lifted during removal exceed 25 kg? No component weights are supplied; if one does, a supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment are required. [C15]",
    "Does bearing inspection or the resolved temperature assessment establish wear, noise or high temperature? If so, both bearings must be replaced as a pair; the standard allowance would be 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, and drive-end HF3-512 and non-drive-end HF3-510 would be required. [C05, C10, C12]"
  ]
}
